# LinkedIn crawl safety

- Never log, echo, or persist cookie/token *values* (`li_at`, CSRF, etc.). Existence checks only.
- Open LinkedIn tabs via the minimized worker window (`createWorkerTab`), not the user's focused window.
- Default sync to paused; require explicit user action to crawl.
- One crawl tab at a time; randomized delays between actions; stop on login/checkpoint/authwall/rate-limit.
- Prefer incremental sync + resume cursors over full re-fetches.
- Graph payloads go to IndexedDB / local `data/` — never commit dumps.
